 "notes": "Das PP et al., J Pure Appl Microbiol 2023;17(3):1591-1604. Assam Medical College & Hospital, Dibrugarh (institution-wide, AMRSN/ICMR site). Study period Oct 2018-Mar 2021. All susceptibility data reported as %RESISTANT (R%) in Table 2 (Gram-negatives) and Table 3 (Gram-positives); every cell converted to %S = 100 - R with from_R:true. Table 2 organisms labelled Klebsiella spp./Proteus spp./Enterobacter spp. mapped to K. pneumoniae/P. mirabilis/E. cloacae with per-cell notes (Klebsiella predominantly K. pneumoniae per abstract). Citrobacter kept as genus. n values taken from Table 2 headers (Acinetobacter n=687, Pseudomonas n=646); note text on p.9 gives slightly different NFGNB counts (A. baumannii n=550, P. aeruginosa n=590). Cefepime, Tobramycin (except Pseudomonas), Minocycline (except Acinetobacter) etc. were ND (not done) for several organisms and omitted. Colistin: MIC-tested on only 261 pooled GN isolates, all susceptible (not organism-specific, so not added per organism). S. aureus vancomycin s=100 added because text states VRSA not detected. MRSA 44.7% = cefoxitin resistance. VRE overall 1",
